+# R24 / 0.1.11 E2LB evidence review — 2026-11-25
+
+Status: experimental source candidate; not a confirmed E2LB connection fix. Based on the 0.1.10 round-2 source archive (which itself has not passed full Android CI), not on the installed 0.1.9 APK. Installed 0.1.9 SHA-256 matches the supplied Nov 25 report: 2c9843711a6cf9c08640e95401b5efd27231ee57de76e6aa8e13f31b60c344be.
+
+## Observations and causal limits
+
+The Nov 25 report contains five availability windows, one single-group and four dual-group, all with 8 DETECT, 0 checksum-valid normal link frames, and zero header/payload/length/noise parser errors within eight seconds. Last positive cumulative ACK before 0x4300 is 109; 0x4300 has sequence 110. This proves neither delivery to the receiver application nor acceptance. Periodic DETECT indicates probe traffic; it does not establish whether the receiver deliberately reset, rejected a request, returned to negotiation, or changed application state. Four attempts were user-stopped; one was ongoing when exported. No full 180-second expiry is demonstrated. R22's speculative gateway SETUP returned 500; R23 removed that fallback for E2LB, so the different symptom is not an improvement in real connectivity.
+
+The accessory certificate and challenge response are still unverified. The source sends a compatibility auth signal; this is not verified authentication or CarPlay authorization. Do not substitute synthetic identifiers, forged certificates, or success signals for real verification. No trusted MFi roots, verified challenge algorithm or successful native iPhone trace is available in these materials. The underlying E2LB launch refusal/absence of response is unresolved. Bluetooth identity is manually configured and not independently verified; its correctness remains unknown. Network-local mDNS registration does not establish peer visibility. No confirmed AirPlay endpoint or invite exists in the observed attempts. CarWith, capture, video, audio, and touch never began, so their behavior cannot explain these failures.
+
+## Changes delivered
+
+- Iap2LinkEngine: passive single-control receipt observes QUEUED, FRAME_GENERATED, PEER_ACKED, ENDED; only a valid cumulative ACK covering that actual sequence confirms the receipt. No changed 0x4300 body, additional retransmission or auth behavior. No-ACK transport retains prior behavior. Malformed FF55 prefixes no longer wait unnecessarily; matching partial marker preserved.
+- Iap2LinkChannel: atomic snapshot of received frame count, parser statistics, liveness and receipt; baseline taken under same lock as submission. Distinguish output generation from actual application acceptance. A write failure cannot produce a successful submission result.
+- Iap2AvailabilityProgress: DETECT_ONLY requires at least three complete markers, zero additional checksum-valid frames, zero new parser errors/noise and FRAME_GENERATED receipt. This threshold is a conservative project policy, NOT a protocol-defined reset condition. Queued control, terminated link, ordinary silence, link activity and explicit start remain separate.
+- Iap2SenderSession: E2LB-only policy stops the observed DETECT_ONLY / NOT_TRANSMITTED branch before delivering an unsupported endpoint, except if another legitimate invitation or accessory Wi-Fi configuration exists. Ended E2LB link is reported as such. Existing Bluetooth teardown/reconnect guard used; no added retry loop or injected SYN. Existing 8-second observation window retained. Potential regression: a valid late start arriving after the guard may be lost; native receiver validation required. Non-E2LB routing preserved, subject to Android CI.
+- Version 0.1.11, versionCode 1110000; local build helper updated to require the installed 0.1.9 certificate fingerprint (44368f6b284b613c5e297d305dbe09f1fd684cf930fce3bebe809c4460b31512). No private keys or passwords in archive. No signed APK produced in this run.
+
+## Validation and limits
+
+32 targeted Kotlin test methods passed using Kotlin 1.9/JDK 21 and minimal JUnit API shims, not the real Gradle JUnit runner. Production link engine, CSM, channel and progress policy compiled; test-only DuplexStream copy uses equivalent ArrayDeque.add instead of addLast due local compiler/JDK interop. New tests cover own ACK vs stale/future ACK, backlogged receipt, wraparound, link end, marker/noise parsing, five identical log-summary windows, alternate handoff and threaded in-memory receipt. These windows reproduce the *observed counters*, not the complete raw vehicle wire protocol. Actual sender integration and Android lifecycle not fully executed. Python 87/87 passed. Full Android build attempt failed because Gradle wrapper cannot resolve services.gradle.org; Android SDK also absent. 0.1.10 inherited changes need CI too. No physical car test. This is a safer failure/recovery policy and diagnostic improvement, not proof of interoperability.
+
+## Acceptance gate (before claiming repaired connection)
+
+1. Parked vehicle: verify supported native wireless CarPlay works on the same receiver/firmware; if it fails, diagnose receiver settings, firmware and official supported setup first. Use authorized diagnostics to establish state milestones, not raw keys or credentials. Establish actual phone Bluetooth identity through supported OS APIs or user-verified system settings.
+2. Verify the legitimate MFi/protocol authentication against the relevant trusted specification and certificate roots; distinguish accessory verification from receiver authorization. Do not mark unverified evidence successful. Compare normal supported session's transport and application stage ordering.
+3. Controlled receiver / bench tests: startup signal delivery and ACK attribution, split/merged/malformed frames, reset/late start, no-ACK negotiation, validated endpoint, stale observations, bounded retry and cancellation; preserve supported older receivers.
+4. Full Android standard and remote test suites, lint, release build, package/version/signature checks. Only use the existing long-term signing key for in-place upgrade. Publish update only after authorized release with digest.
+5. Real E2LB repeated cold/warm starts, 0x4301 or other legitimate receiver startup evidence, verified endpoint, SETUP and RECORD success, actual image/sound/touch and reconnect. Until then do not claim the car is fixed.
